-\begin{question}
+\begin{question}\label{mmp-001V}
 Can the set of slice knots detect exotic smooth structures? In other words, do there exist smooth, homeomorphic four-manifolds $X$ and $X'$ and a knot $K \subset S^3$ that is slice in $X$ but not in $X'$?
 \end{question}
 
 Finally, in view of Corollaries~\ref{cor:exotica} and \ref{cor:DV}, we propose the following problem.
 
-\begin{question}
+\begin{question}\label{mmp-001W}
 Is it true that for every closed $4$-manifold $X$, there is a knot $K$ that is topologically but not smoothly H-slice in $X$?
 \end{question}
 
